    "product_experience_officer": {
      "type": "av-product-experience-officer",
      "blocks": {
        "amazon_review_1": {
          "type": "testimonial",
          "settings": {
            "image_alt": "Amazon review image 1",
            "asset_filename": "av-peo-amazon-review-1.jpg",
            "title": "Monet-inspired and made to last",
            "text": "The tiles are beautiful. The reference and design reflect one of my favorite artist Monet and my love of gardening.\n\nThe bird bam is a hummingbird, the jokers are the dragonflies, and even the dragon carry the garden flare.\n\nThe tiles are a quality pieces and will hold up well to the monthly games with my friends. Quality time with friends with a game pieces that will last for years is value for the money.\n\nThe size is a little larger than the standard tile. (Included a piece comparing the joker and a blank tile for reference. ) The standard tile is about 0.5 inches verse these tiles of 0.75 inches. There is no difference in the width and height between these tiles and standard tiles, so no impact for building your walls."
          }
        },
        "amazon_review_2": {
          "type": "testimonial",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/3_6cee787c-7844-442b-83df-a7bb8be77176.jpg",
            "image_alt": "Amazon review image 2",
            "asset_filename": "av-peo-amazon-review-2.jpg",
            "title": "Great purchase and value",
            "text": "Great purchase. I have a very expensive set of tiles and I would challenge anyone to tell the difference in these in quality. The orange is a soft orange that I really like. More of a sherbet color. They are easy to read. A great value for the money."
          }
        },
        "amazon_review_3": {
          "type": "testimonial",
          "settings": {
            "image_alt": "Amazon review image 3",
            "asset_filename": "av-peo-amazon-review-3.jpg",
            "title": "Pretty apricot color and solid quality",
            "text": "The tiles are this pretty apricot color, kind of a soft warm orange that looks fresh and modern. They feel good in your hand-decent weight, smooth edges, and they don't feel cheap at all. I've shuffled and built walls with them a bunch and they hold up well, no chips or scratches showing up yet.\n\nThe pictures and symbols on the tiles are bright and easy to read. The dots, bamboos, and characters stand out sharply against the white background, so you can spot what you need quickly even if the room isn't super bright. The winds, dragons, and flowers have nice clear colors too, which makes the whole set fun to look at while you're playing.\n\nAll in all, it's a solid set that doesn't cost a ton but still looks good and works great. The extra cards are a big help for new players, and the nice color and clear designs make it more enjoyable than a lot of basic sets out there. Perfect for family nights or casual games with friends."
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "amazon_review_1",
        "amazon_review_2",
        "amazon_review_3"
      ],
